<title>USA: TABLE - DQE Inc Q2 net up with gain.</title>
<headline>TABLE - DQE Inc Q2 net up with gain.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>(All figures in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			   Second Quarter	    12 Months</p>
<p>			 1997 (a)    1996	1997 (a)     1996</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>    revenues     $284,000  $293,357  $1,219,904   $1,232,387</p>
<p> Net income	 $46,778   $38,972    $189,736     $175,254</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>    outstanding    77,394    77,392	77,275	 77,514</p>
<p> Earnings per share $0.61     $0.50	 $2.46	  $2.27</p>
<p>(a)  Reflects $0.09 per share gain from sale of Chester</p>
<p>Engineers.</p>
<p>Duquesne Light Co, an electric utility, is the largest of the DQE subsidiaries, and had the following sales in millions of kilowatt-hours for the periods indicated.</p>
<p>Direct Sales:</p>
<p>    Residential	 697	 743	 3,253	  3,477</p>
<p>    Commercial	1,338     1,393	 5,663	  5,810</p>
<p>    Industrial	  875	 793	 3,382	  3,245</p>
<p>    Other		  20	  20	    83	     83</p>
<p>Total sales to</p>
<p>    customers	 2,930     2,949	12,381	 12,615</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
